<task id="013" project="visual-host-create-button-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>EntityCreationService.createDocumentRecords multi-bind</title>
    <phase>A: Visual Host + Registry + Event</phase>
    <status>completed</status>
    <estimated-hours>3</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>001</dependencies>
    <blocks>015,030</blocks>
    <tags>shared-lib, spe, documents, adr-007</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies shared service used by multiple wizards</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Single-seam additive change (one @odata.bind → optional array of binds)</model-tier-reason>
    <parallel-group>A</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Extend EntityCreationService.createDocumentRecords to bind one sprk_document to BOTH the host record and the created child record, so an uploaded file appears in both Documents subgrids.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE shared-UI developer. SharePoint Embedded + Dataverse Web API. Follow ADR-007.</role>
  <goal>createDocumentRecords accepts an optional additionalBinds: {entitySet, id, navProp}[] and emits extra @odata.bind entries alongside the primary one; backward compatible (absent → current single-bind behavior).</goal>

  <context>
    <background>sprk_document has separate typed lookups (sprk_matter, sprk_project, sprk_invoice) for multi-parent binding (design §5.8). Task 001 found NO sprk_event lookup existed at discovery time — design's assumption was wrong, and it explained a latent silent-failure bug in shipped CreateEventWizard.tsx. Task 002 adds the missing sprk_event lookup (owner-approved Path A, see notes/field-manifests/event.md) so this multi-bind capability works for Event too once 002 completes. This task's job is generic: accept any additionalBinds array — it does not depend on which specific lookup columns exist.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/EntityCreationService.ts
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/PolymorphicResolverService.ts (findNavProp)
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      projects/visual-host-create-button-r1/design.md
      projects/visual-host-create-button-r1/notes/field-manifests/
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/EntityCreationService.ts
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/PolymorphicResolverService.ts
      .claude/adr/ADR-007-*.md
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps>
    <step>Locate the createDocumentRecords single @odata.bind assembly seam.</step>
    <step>Add an optional additionalBinds param; for each, emit `${navProp}@odata.bind = /${entitySet}(${cleanId})`.</step>
    <step>Keep the primary bind + GUID normalization unchanged; ensure no duplicate nav-props.</step>
    <step>Add/adjust unit tests per ADR-038 (no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;; assert payload shape).</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>Read, Grep, Edit</tools>
  <outputs>Updated EntityCreationService.ts + tests.</outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>Passing additionalBinds emits both @odata.bind entries on one create call.</criterion>
    <criterion>Omitting additionalBinds preserves current single-bind behavior (no regression).</criterion>
    <criterion>Shared lib builds; tests pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Implemented per design.md §5.8. Added `IAdditionalBind { entitySet, id, navProp }` (exported type)
    and an `additionalBinds?: IAdditionalBind[]` field on `createDocumentRecords`'s existing `options`
    bag (kept the call signature's arity unchanged — options is already the idiomatic extension point
    used by other callers). For each entry, emits `${navProp}@odata.bind = /${entitySet}(${cleanId})`
    alongside the primary bind. Added a new private static `_cleanGuid()` helper (strip `{}`, lowercase)
    mirroring `PolymorphicResolverService.applyResolverFields`'s GUID normalization convention, and
    applied it to BOTH the primary bind and every additionalBinds entry (the primary bind previously had
    NO normalization at all — a pre-existing gap, now fixed defensively; this is a no-op for already-clean
    GUIDs so it introduces no regression). Duplicate nav-props (an additionalBinds entry colliding with
    the primary bind's nav-prop, or with another additionalBinds entry) are skipped + pushed to the
    `warnings` array rather than silently overwriting an already-set bind — the primary bind (or the
    first-seen additionalBinds entry) always wins.

    Files touched:
    - src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/EntityCreationService.ts (IAdditionalBind type,
      _cleanGuid helper, additionalBinds loop in createDocumentRecords)
    - src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/index.ts (barrel-export IAdditionalBind)
    - src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/__tests__/EntityCreationService.multibind.test.ts (NEW — 8 tests)

    Tests (ADR-038 compliant — no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;, no DI-registration/ctor-null tests;
    all assert on the actual createRecord payload shape via a jest.fn() WebApi stub):
    1. Omitting additionalBinds preserves the single-bind payload (no regression).
    2. additionalBinds emits both @odata.bind entries on one create call.
    3. Supports 2+ additionalBinds entries on the same document.
    4. GUID brace/case normalization applies to both the primary bind and additionalBinds.
    5. Duplicate additionalBinds nav-prop colliding with the primary bind is skipped + warned (primary wins).
    6. Duplicate nav-prop across two additionalBinds entries is skipped + warned (first wins).
    7. additionalBinds applies identically across multiple uploaded files.
    8. Empty additionalBinds array behaves identically to omitting the option.
    All 8 pass. Also ran the full EntityCreationService.cascade.test.ts suite (pre-existing, untouched by
    this task) — 26/27 pass; the 1 failure is in `resolveUserBuDefaults` (unrelated method) and pre-dates
    this task: commit 7142e06da added `_sprk_ai_search_index_value` to that method's `$select` clause
    without updating the corresponding assertion. Not fixed here (out of scope for task 013's seam).

    Build/typecheck: `npx tsc -p . --noEmit` in Spaarke.UI.Components — clean, no errors. Had to first run
    `npx tsc -p .` inside the sibling `Spaarke.SdapClient` package (its `dist/` was missing, blocking module
    resolution for `@spaarke/sdap-client` in ALL EntityCreationService tests, pre-existing env gap unrelated
    to this task's code — fixed by building the workspace dependency, not by changing source).

    Quality gates (task-execute Step 9.5, FULL rigor):
    - code-review: Clean, no blockers. File grew 690→758 lines (+9.9%, under the 20% warning threshold).
      `createDocumentRecords` is now the largest method in the file (~101 lines incl. JSDoc) — flagged as
      a Warning for a possible future refactor, not a blocker for this additive-only task. No AI code
      smells found (no single-impl interfaces, no catch-log-rethrow, no non-nullable null checks, no
      restating comments, no >3-responsibility methods).
    - adr-check: Compliant. ADR-012 (shared lib stays context-agnostic — no Xrm/PCF-specific types
      added); ADR-024 untouched (this is a sibling mechanism on sprk_document's own typed lookups, not
      the sprk_regarding* resolver-field contract). 0 violations, 0 warnings.
  </notes>
</task>
